<% if @blockchain_connection.ethereum? %>
  <h1>Add an Ethereum wallet</h1>
  <p>
    Track a self-custody Ethereum address from public chain data: its ETH, including ETH paid out
    by contracts, and the gas fees it pays. Paste the address (<code>0x</code> followed by 40
    characters). Never paste a private key or seed phrase; Honeyledger only needs public data.
  </p>
  <p>
    The explorer the server queries sees which address it looks up. Token balances are not tracked yet.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <h1>Add a Bitcoin wallet</h1>
  <p>
    Track a self-custody wallet from public chain data. Paste a single address, or the wallet's
    extended public key (<code>xpub</code>, <code>ypub</code>, or <code>zpub</code>) to follow every
    address it uses. Never paste a private key or seed phrase; Honeyledger only needs public data.
  </p>
  <p>
    An extended public key reveals the wallet's full history to whoever holds it, and the explorer
    the server queries sees which addresses it looks up. The server's operator can point it at a
    self-hosted explorer to keep those lookups private.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>xpub</code> keys are read as legacy (1…) wallets. If your wallet uses native SegWit
    (bc1q…), export its <code>zpub</code>; for nested SegWit (3…), its <code>ypub</code>.
  </p>
<% end %>

<%= form_with model: @blockchain_connection, url: blockchain_connections_path, method: :post, local: true do |form| %>
  <%= render "blockchain/connections/errors", connection: @blockchain_connection %>

  <%= form.hidden_field :chain %>

  <div class="field">
    <%= form.label :name, "Label" %><br>
    <%= form.text_field :name, placeholder: "Cold storage" %>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <%= form.label :identifier, @blockchain_connection.ethereum? ? "Address" : "Address or extended public key" %><br>
    <%= form.text_field :identifier, autocomplete: "off", spellcheck: false, size: 60 %>
  </div>

  <div class="actions">
    <%= form.submit "Add wallet" %>
  </div>
<% end %>
